WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.230
What's wrong, Hakone?

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:09.900
Lately, lots of people have been illegally downloading TV shows over the internet.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:18.080
Without the rights owner's permission, distribution via bootlegs is illegal!

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:23.160
Please... remember that...

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.380
Days start very early for the Charging Ladies.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:34.720
Even for citizens living in a hi-tech parallel world,

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:38.470
a working society is still the norm.

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:49.400
Please wake up!

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:31.610
Yikes! Who turned off the alarm clock?!

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:34.400
Today, the Charging Ladies will continue to make progress!

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:40.520
Kiseki wa genjitsu no tonari ni aru

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:40.520
Miracles are right beside reality

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:43.610
Kanarazu aru

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:43.610
They're there for sure

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:54.960
Chiisana tameiki shinpai dakara

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:54.960
I heave a tiny sigh because I'm worried

00:01:55.330 --> 00:02:00.870
Ushiro sugata mimamotteirunda yo

00:01:55.330 --> 00:02:00.870
From behind you, I'm watching over you

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:06.810
Kirai dattara konna koto iwanai yo

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:06.810
I wouldn't be saying this if I hated you

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:12.990
Kitto hito wa hitori janai

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:12.990
I know it must be true that no man is an island

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:14.400
Hitori janai

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:14.400
You're not alone

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:20.670
Tatoeba sotto yubisaki ni fureru omoi

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:20.670
For example, if you gently brush those hopes with your fingertips

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:26.610
Tatoeba taisetsu na toki wo wasurenaide

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:26.610
For example, if you never forget these precious times

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:32.550
Kakato wo motto sukoshi dake takaku agete

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:32.550
I'll boost you up, just a little higher

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:38.530
Mieru yo ano ko no hitomi ni utsuru hikari

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:38.530
Look and see the light reflecting in her eyes

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:44.400
ENERGY wa sekai no zenbu ni michiteru

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:44.400
Filling up the whole world with energy

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:52.190
Ima dake wa chikara wo kashite ageru yo

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:52.190
Just for now, I'll lend my strength to you

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:07.790
We're off!

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:09.540
Take care of yourselves!

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:11.120
Got it!

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:18.300
And then, brother went "Hey!" in a fit of rage.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.590
He sounded like a gangster.

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:21.930
"Gangsta Bro."

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:24.850
<i>Hakone, you seem to be much better now.</i>

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:28.020
What's wrong, Iono? What's with the grin?

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:30.440
W-What grin?

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:34.060
Is someone on your mind?

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:36.230
What sort of things were you
thinking to make you grin like that?

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:47.540
Alright, I can do this too!

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.630
Timing!

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.540
Timing!

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:02.590
I'll be eaten!

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:04.930
So tight!

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:06.010
Milly!

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:09.970
B-Bitch...

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.770
Show some spunk, you spineless wretch!

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:16.270
Don't you go crying on me!

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:17.730
What are you moaning for?!

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:19.400
You call yourself the Magical Girl of Love?!

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:23.820
Stop it...

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.370
It feels so good!

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.910
Whoops! Time for work.

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:33.160
I can't take it anymore!

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:40.260
Target sighted!

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:43.170
Now where's the power supply...

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:44.430
Out of the way!

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:46.930
Charge.

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:50.600
Alesta!

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.850
Why are you here?!

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:54.560
Isn't this area out of your jurisdiction?

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.730
Why, you ask? Don't you get it?

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:57.860
Obviously not!

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:04.030
It's because a certain someone can't fulfill simple tasks, so the Captain gave me a call.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:06.870
I'll be adjusting the balance in this area for a while.

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:09.330
Even if you say that, to waltz in so suddenly is...

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:12.790
Do you know what this is?

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:15.580
This is you-know-who's stats for this month.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:17.000
Failed charge-ups: 6.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.790
Cases involving destruction of equipment: 2.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:22.590
Also, 3 warnings in one month.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:24.840
Got anything to say?

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:27.220
Not that I care, anyway.

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:32.810
I'm here to help, so do me a favor and go some place where you won't be a nuisance.

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:37.060
What gives?! That pisses me off!

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:40.360
Just because your record is a little better than mine, you're all cocky!

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:45.490
Idiot! Dumbass! Cold-blooded, irritating four-eyes!

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.000
I better get to work.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:01.290
Maybe I should get this pair of tickets.

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:04.300
Although it would be easier to invite
him if Hakone came along...

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:14.930
Depression level C, let's go!

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:16.230
Charge.

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:18.600
I feel great!

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:20.520
I haven't lost yet...

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:25.690
Yes! This time, I'll definitely...

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:26.900
Charge.

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:30.110
I feel so refreshed!

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.490
Charge.

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:43.670
Charge.

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:08.570
Hell yeah!

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:10.820
What was that for?!

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:12.780
You just punched a girl in the face!

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:14.870
It's better than getting hit by a baseball bat.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:16.290
What are you talking about?

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.500
Forget that, just don't get in the way of my work.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:22.080
Get in the way? That's my line!

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:25.090
You've been stealing the targets
I found that needed to be charged.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:27.760
How can you accuse me of stealing?

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:30.260
You're just a slowpoke, am I wrong?

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:31.970
That is...

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:36.010
Charge them immediately upon detection;
isn't that what the Captain's been telling us?

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:39.480
Really, you're giving me more than a hit on the face.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:42.520
Being colleagues with a failure like you is the worst.

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:46.400
Do you know what they call you in the company?

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:48.940
Miss Pay Cut, Master of Lame Excuses,

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:50.450
and Queen of Screw-ups.

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:56.490
It's such a pain to be categorized in the same class as you.

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:59.830
You aren't suited for this line of work.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:07.130
That target...

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:12.430
I charged him up a year ago.

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:16.510
Again? There seems to be a lot of repeaters lately.

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:19.890
Guess I have no choice.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:23.230
What a pity, my shift is over.

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:24.600
You're heading back?!

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:29.070
Of course, I don't do overtime.
Besides, I still have things to do.

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:30.940
See you.

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:47.130
Bitch...!

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:51.050
What's with you, looking all slutty?!

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:52.970
You're a disgrace to all Magical Girls!

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:54.970
Forgive me!

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:01.220
The stealth device...

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:09.110
Sentou.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:12.190
Once you're done with that,
please go sweep up the back.

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:13.610
Sure, boss.

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:26.620
Wh-What's up?

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.790
I'll go sweep now!

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:34.550
That was very mean!

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:37.090
Blame it on your sudden peekaboo-through-the-wall routine.

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:40.430
I didn't even know you worked here!

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:42.930
Then, why are you here for?

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:45.520
To charge up a customer, or something?

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:49.270
No, that's not it...

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:50.860
It isn't?

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:52.690
Yeah... I guess so...

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:56.400
Hey, did something happen?

00:09:57.160 --> 00:10:01.530
Well, you just seem a little gloomier than usual,
so I was wondering if something was bothering you.

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:06.040
For example, being a burden to a
colleague and getting yelled at?

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:09.630
Bullseye.

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:15.550
That's... actually...

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:24.520
That's why I think...
maybe I'm not really cut out for this sort of job.

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:26.180
I wouldn't know.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:29.060
But...

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:35.900
This is just my opinion.
It's nothing profound, so don't expect much.

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:37.030
I get it already.

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:40.620
For example, the job you guys do...

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:42.390
Visual Guide to Charging

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:42.390
This booklet is a work of fiction

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:45.250
Let's say there is a victim and an abuser.

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:48.710
Even if you recharge the victim's energy,

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:51.580
it won't change what the abuser does.

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:58.050
If that were the case, then the situation hasn't changed, and in the end it'd still be bad.

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:02.010
That's why the repeaters, as you
call them will reappear, right?

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:06.270
The point is you're only fixing the problem on the surface.

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:09.480
It's just like changing the batteries of a toy that ran out.

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:12.150
Old battery out, new battery in, and it's done.

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:16.570
Well, in my opinion, it's something you should feel good about doing.

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:19.820
But it's just a job for you guys, so it doesn't matter, right?

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:21.070
What's with that?!

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:23.240
Are you trying to pick a fight?!

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:25.830
What're you getting so angry about? I only said what was on my mind.

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:29.910
It's not like that! Our job isn't like that!

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:31.920
You clearly don't know anything!

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:36.050
Even I'm... Even I'm doing my best!

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:36.050
Hey, cut it out.

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:38.010
Why you...

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:48.730
I'm just handing this ticket to him,
it's really nothing, nothing at all...

00:11:57.820 --> 00:11:59.190
Senny-

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:00.820
Don't screw with me!

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:03.240
Just because you're a girl who passes through walls...!

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:06.910
Really annoying! It pisses me off!

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:09.370
You listen here, this is the back of the store...

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:12.210
I can beat the hell outta you here!

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:12.750
I don't care anymore! You're the worst!

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:16.380
You useless office lady!

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:28.060
Just a little bit.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.020
Amazing!

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:40.520
I can't believe he was like that...

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:44.720
Just who was the one that saved Hakone?

00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:47.580
Who was it?

00:12:49.010 --> 00:12:56.880
It was through his scoldings that I eventually found the reason for Hakone's depression.

00:12:56.880 --> 00:13:00.060
Then, working with him...

00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:04.220
But, if it had been only me...

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:08.630
...would I have been able to save Hakone...?

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:14.080
Okay!

00:13:56.820 --> 00:13:58.440
There he is.

00:14:21.110 --> 00:14:22.780
I'm home.

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:26.630
I'm so sorry this all we have for dinner, Akihiro.

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:29.180
But hey, no better time to eat a pork chop, right?

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:31.490
Good luck for tomorrow's entrance exam!

00:14:31.490 --> 00:14:33.850
If you're nervous, you can't answer the questions that you normally could.

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:37.580
Don't worry. Your brother passed it,
so there's no reason you can't!

00:14:42.370 --> 00:14:46.750
In the end, I still can't even get a B.

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:49.280
If I don't pass this time, it'll be the fourth time.

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:53.790
It would have been great if I was told to go work before I became like this...

00:14:53.790 --> 00:14:57.520
Then I wouldn't have had to suffer
so much over these questions.

00:14:58.470 --> 00:15:01.070
They don't understand me at all.

00:15:01.070 --> 00:15:03.420
What's it even mean to work hard? Dammit!

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:08.170
If I were to charge him in his current condition...

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:12.950
...he might become hostile towards the people who were supporting him.

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:15.070
It's exactly how he said.

00:15:15.070 --> 00:15:19.020
Just like changing the battery of a toy.

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:22.880
Then, this time...

00:15:30.180 --> 00:15:31.680
Good luck to you!

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:44.370
The exam venue is over here!

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:46.710
Sign: "University entrance exam venue"

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:48.890
<i>With the test paper in front of him,</i>

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:51.740
<i>even if he's down, he'll have to move on.</i>

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:54.240
<i>If I'm going to charge him up,
that would be the time to do so.</i>

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:58.370
<i>Just a little more, then I will...</i>

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:05.310
Wait. Hey... where are you going?

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:06.650
Hey, wait!

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:10.400
Don't tell me... has he totally given up?!

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:19.830
It wouldn't matter anyway.
Anything I do will be futile.

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:26.840
I can't believe he's doing this...

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:29.130
He's even smoking!

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:31.460
Repeating three times makes him twenty-one.

00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:33.150
So what if he smokes?

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:38.980
Don't scare me like that...

00:16:38.980 --> 00:16:41.000
That wasn't my intention.

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:44.300
But seeing your pathetic state really makes my day.

00:16:44.300 --> 00:16:45.520
Why are you here?

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:49.090
What brought me here? Today and tomorrow are the university entrance exams.

00:16:49.090 --> 00:16:52.130
A lot of people come to take the
test while they're feeling depressed.

00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:57.120
There are so many signals all over the place!

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:59.140
It really is a problematic situation.

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:01.950
There must be over a hundred people.

00:17:02.850 --> 00:17:05.650
And he's the only one left.

00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:09.920
Y-You can't!

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:13.330
If you charge him up now,
it will become a vicious cycle!

00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:15.290
You need to have good timing!

00:17:15.290 --> 00:17:16.430
What timing?

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:20.260
If we leave him like that,
if we're late by one second, what do we do?

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:21.770
That...

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:23.940
No point talking to you.

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:26.710
But you can't! You mustn't!

00:17:26.710 --> 00:17:27.680
Let go!

00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:29.620
Anything is fine now.

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:33.270
Depression level rose from C to B!

00:17:33.270 --> 00:17:35.390
I'm going to go charge him up!

00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:36.530
I told you to wait a moment!

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:37.910
Let go!

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:38.680
No way!

00:17:38.680 --> 00:17:40.210
Damn!

00:17:43.050 --> 00:17:44.290
What the hell are you doing?!

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:52.410
To us they may just be charging targets...

00:17:52.410 --> 00:17:55.710
...but that guy is just like us!

00:17:55.710 --> 00:17:57.610
He can feel pain, he can worry,

00:17:57.610 --> 00:18:00.630
but there are people who will support and cheer for him!

00:18:00.630 --> 00:18:03.420
He's a human being with feelings!

00:18:03.940 --> 00:18:07.770
Oh yeah, that manga café should be open by now.

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:11.230
You can't!

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:15.280
Don't you still have your family who's
supporting you by your side?!

00:18:21.490 --> 00:18:25.000
Lucky Charm

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:58.470
Charge!

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:16.840
Where am I?

00:19:17.810 --> 00:19:21.230
There's only five minutes left 'til the exam starts!

00:19:21.230 --> 00:19:22.860
This is bad!

00:19:23.460 --> 00:19:27.330
This time for sure! University or bust!

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:35.520
I did it!

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:39.850
I did it!

00:19:39.850 --> 00:19:42.110
What you did...

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:45.480
How dare you use my face as a springboard!

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:49.210
Thanks to you, I got to jump to the rescue! Thanks!

00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:51.960
Then, how about this ending?

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:56.700
How is it? Hey, what do you think?

00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:01.010
You seem to be misunderstanding something, so I'll be kind and tell you.

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:02.750
I misunderstood?

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:06.140
Our job is to charge people up, then collect our salary.

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:07.310
That's...

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:10.440
Maybe you can save people,

00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:15.650
but if there's really a need to,
why would there be a quota?

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:19.840
All you did was save one person out of the crowd.

00:20:19.840 --> 00:20:21.570
That's the reality.

00:20:22.100 --> 00:20:23.850
And just now...

00:20:23.850 --> 00:20:27.130
...if the lucky charm hadn't somehow
fallen out of his pocket...

00:20:27.130 --> 00:20:29.010
...could you have saved him?

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:35.290
I knew it, you really are not suited for this job.

00:20:53.090 --> 00:20:56.340
<i>It might be like Alesta says.</i>

00:20:56.340 --> 00:21:02.200
<i>But I don't want to believe that the lucky charm falling out was a coincidence.</i>

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:06.900
<i>It was saying... "This boy... I'm counting on you."</i>

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:15.770
The university entrance exam for the second day ended.

00:21:15.770 --> 00:21:18.890
Fully confident with his answers,

00:21:18.890 --> 00:21:22.260
Akihiro let out a smile full of assurance and happiness.

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:26.810
Now then, let's work hard for today as well!

00:21:26.810 --> 00:21:28.430
Up, up and away!

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:39.920
So... what?

00:21:39.920 --> 00:21:42.030
My way of thinking isn't wrong.

00:21:42.030 --> 00:21:43.570
Definitely not!

00:22:20.010 --> 00:22:21.660
Damn that Plug...

00:22:21.660 --> 00:22:24.760
I told her to not randomly appear out of nowhere...

00:22:24.760 --> 00:22:28.530
But... the impact felt kinda different...

00:22:29.460 --> 00:22:31.140
Oh well, forget it.

00:22:35.920 --> 00:22:39.400
Honto wa totemo TOUGH nan da yo

00:22:35.920 --> 00:22:39.400
Really, I'm quite tough, you know

00:22:39.400 --> 00:22:42.200
Hitori demo heiki de

00:22:39.400 --> 00:22:42.200
I'm fine even all by myself

00:22:42.200 --> 00:22:44.970
Doko ni demo ikeru no

00:22:42.200 --> 00:22:44.970
I can go anywhere at all

00:22:44.970 --> 00:22:47.730
Koibito nante iranai

00:22:44.970 --> 00:22:47.730
I don't need a boyfriend or anything

00:22:47.730 --> 00:22:53.230
Takumashiku ikiteikunda to kimetetanda

00:22:47.730 --> 00:22:53.230
I decided that I would live strong

00:22:53.230 --> 00:22:54.990
Kimi to deau made wa

00:22:53.230 --> 00:22:54.990
Until the day I could meet you

00:23:00.230 --> 00:23:03.000
Sore wa arigachi na

00:23:00.230 --> 00:23:03.000
"That really is

00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:05.790
Warui kuse da yo

00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:05.790
It's a bad habit

00:23:05.790 --> 00:23:08.560
Hanashi janai ka? nante

00:23:05.790 --> 00:23:08.560
such an often-heard saying, right?"

00:23:08.560 --> 00:23:11.360
Toshiue buranaide ne

00:23:08.560 --> 00:23:11.360
Don't pretend to be older than you are

00:23:11.360 --> 00:23:16.520
Datte ne watashi wa itsumo tokubetsu

00:23:11.360 --> 00:23:16.520
But you know, I'm always an exceptional case

00:23:16.890 --> 00:23:19.660
Kimi ni mo kitto SPECIAL deshou

00:23:16.890 --> 00:23:19.660
I'm sure I'm special to you, too

00:23:19.660 --> 00:23:21.380
Sore de nakya iya

00:23:19.660 --> 00:23:21.380
I couldn't stand it any other way

00:23:21.730 --> 00:23:25.200
Zettai watashi soba ni iru yo

00:23:21.730 --> 00:23:25.200
I'll definitely always be beside you

00:23:25.200 --> 00:23:33.230
Kimi ga ochikondara namida fusegu kasa ni naritainda yo

00:23:25.200 --> 00:23:29.230
I want to become the umbrella

00:23:29.230 --> 00:23:33.230
that shields you from tears when you're feeling down

00:23:33.530 --> 00:23:38.800
Keredo mamoreteru no wa naze ka watashi bakari

00:23:33.530 --> 00:23:38.800
But why is it that I'm the one who always ends up being protected?

00:23:39.120 --> 00:23:45.090
Kimochi no naka no koishi ne tsumazuite korobisou na toki

00:23:39.120 --> 00:23:45.090
At the times when, in my heart, I stumble and seem about to fall

00:23:45.300 --> 00:23:49.820
Itsumo sotto sasaete kureru

00:23:45.300 --> 00:23:49.820
Keep supporting me just a little, always

00:23:50.190 --> 00:23:54.330
Futoshita kizuna itoshii yo

00:23:50.190 --> 00:23:54.330
I'll treasure this unexpected bond

00:23:54.330 --> 00:23:55.670
Itsumademo

00:23:54.330 --> 00:23:55.670
Now and forever

00:23:56.050 --> 00:23:59.890
Eien Sweetheart

00:23:56.050 --> 00:23:59.890
Eternally, Sweetheart

00:24:04.460 --> 00:24:07.170
Being a Charging Lady is a tough job!

00:24:07.170 --> 00:24:11.500
But giving depressed people
dreams and hope is an amazing job!

00:24:11.500 --> 00:24:14.060
So how much money are you making?

00:24:14.060 --> 00:24:15.430
Including the overtime.

00:24:15.430 --> 00:24:19.380
Let's leave this kind of problematic question to Alesta...

00:24:19.810 --> 00:24:21.020
What's wrong, Alesta?

00:24:21.020 --> 00:24:22.330
What is this...?

00:24:23.030 --> 00:24:25.480
On the next episode of
Fight In one Strike! Charging Ladies!!:

00:24:24.980 --> 00:24:33.780
Lock On!

00:24:25.480 --> 00:24:26.770
Lock On!

00:24:26.770 --> 00:24:29.240
This kind of unexplainable feeling...

00:24:29.240 --> 00:24:30.850
Just what is happening to my body?!

00:24:31.550 --> 00:24:33.010
Who knows?
